\subsection{\code{BaseRInteractionLayerProcessor$extract_axis_titles()}}{
  The three labels the drawing writes, each explicit argument first.

All three of \code{interaction.plot}'s own defaults are
\code{deparse1(substitute(...))} of an argument, so they name the
\emph{expression} the caller wrote. The wrapper records evaluated values, by
which point \code{substitute()} is long gone -- a factor's levels are not its
name -- so the expressions come off the recorded call text instead, the
way the correlograms recover their series names (#276).
